{:pi "claude-opus-5", :decisions "Two false signals found in the DigitalOcean deploy and fixed. (1) The health gate reported success after 30 consecutive failed probes: verify.sh runs `docker compose exec -T`, which inherited the ssh stdin carrying the gate's own unparsed `bash -s` script, ate the failure branch, and let bash exit 0 at the premature EOF. Every remote heredoc body is now a `{ ... } </dev/null` group and every exec closes stdin, with a code-quality guard asserting both. (2) Knoxx answered 401 request_context_unresolved because KNOXX_API_KEY_USER_EMAIL held an unlisted personal address, and Knoxx resolves API-key identity solely through contracts/knoxx/actors/ — an unlisted address syncs no user and no membership. Added the knoxx_dev_automation actor contract (system-admin, mirroring pi) and repointed the production variable at knoxx-dev-automation@promethean.rest per user instruction. Also wired GitHub OAuth (absent entirely, so no human could log in) and pinned KNOXX_SESSION_SECRET, which the backend otherwise regenerates per process, signing everyone out on each redeploy. Decoupled CADDY_ACME_EMAIL from the API-key identity.", :tests "stdin-consumption bug and the `{ } </dev/null` fix reproduced locally in isolation; code-quality guard fails on the pre-fix tree (2 heredocs + 3 execs) and passes after; all repo yaml parses; bash -n clean across digitalocean/**/*.sh; actionlint reports only the pre-existing SC2029 infos; the new actor contract parses under bb and reads back the expected :actor/email. Not yet redeployed.", :refs ".github/workflows/deploy-digitalocean.yml,.github/workflows/code-quality.yml,contracts/knoxx/actors/knoxx_dev_automation.edn,digitalocean/services/knoxx/{compose.yaml,env.template,verify.sh},digitalocean/services/caddy/{env.template,verify.sh},run 30679331293", :dod "false-green-health-gate-closed; knoxx-api-key-identity-resolvable; oauth-and-session-secret-wired", :manifest "none", :note "No secret values printed or logged. KNOXX_GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID/SECRET were piped from the local pm2 dump straight into the GitHub production environment; KNOXX_SESSION_SECRET freshly generated as 64 hex chars.", :ts "2026-08-01T10:25:08.105Z", :host "local", :drift "The GitHub OAuth app is registered against http://localhost:8000; its Authorization callback URL must become https://knoxx.promethean.rest/api/auth/callback/github or login fails on redirect_uri mismatch. DO_INFERENCE_API_KEY still absent, so proxx embeddings stay disabled.", :kind :decision, :origin "claude-session-resume", :repo "/home/err/spaces/open-hax-services-deployment-infra", :owner "receipt-river"}
{:pi "claude-opus-5", :decisions "Phase 3 done: full DNS cutover and ingress live. Repointed knoxx and proxx A records from the dead 104.130.159.19 to 157.245.125.134, DNS-only so HTTP-01 reaches the origin. Deliberately left openplanner.promethean.rest on the dead IP — OpenPlanner has no HTTP service in this topology and no Caddy site block, so pointing it at the droplet would trade a timeout for a TLS failure. Two further deploy defects of the same family as the health gate found and fixed en route: the proxx Caddy site carried the app repo's /v1*-vs-console split against port 5174, which nothing binds in the production image (one process serves both on 8789), so every non-API path 502'd; and `docker compose up -d` never recreated the caddy container after the Caddyfile changed, because compose hashes image+environment and not bind-mount contents, while rsync's write-and-rename left the file mount pinned to the original inode. Deploys now pass --force-recreate whenever rsync reports the definition moved.", :tests "Verified externally, not from logs: knoxx and proxx both return HTTP 200 over HTTPS with valid Let's Encrypt certificates (CN matches, expires 2026-10-30, ssl_verify_result=0) and 308 from HTTP. Knoxx serves the app shell (<title>Knoxx</title>, id=root); /api/auth/config reports githubEnabled true; unauthenticated /api/config returns 401. GitHub accepts the OAuth authorize request for redirect_uri https://knoxx.promethean.rest/api/auth/callback/github and 302s to sign-in, so the registered callback already matches — no redirect_uri mismatch. proxx /health returns ok:true with the requesty provider registered. Host-side knoxx verify.sh: healthy, proxx reachable, openplanner data plane in-process (sdk), auth enforced. All five containers healthy. caddy health gate passed on its merits.", :refs "open-hax/services#33,#34,#35; runs 30696358354 30696778888 30697023834; digitalocean/services/caddy/Caddyfile,.github/workflows/deploy-digitalocean.yml", :dod "knox